// AUTO-EXPANDED REFERENCE FILE -- generated by macro-expanding every Wave()
// (WinSky "wave shape" DSL) block in pixel/WaveShapes.sky.h into a plain C++ function.
// This file is NOT compiled as part of any build; it exists purely as a
// human-readable porting reference.  Math and variable names are preserved
// verbatim from the source macros (WaveVars a[]/b[]/c[]/x[]/y[] arrays).
//
// Shape count expanded: 192
//
// ---- WaveVars input variables (pixel/WaveVars.h) ----
// a[MaxArray]  (MaxArray=40) -- "setup" scratch registers, evaluated ONCE
//              per instance when a wave shape is first selected (A() macro).
//              Typically holds randomized per-instance constants (radii,
//              phase offsets, seeds, rates) via rnd()/trnc()/sgn() etc.
// b[MaxArray]  -- "frame" scratch registers, evaluated ONCE PER RENDERED
//              FRAME per instance (B() macro).  Typically time-driven state
//              (rotation angles, envelope followers) built from `t` and a[].
// c[MaxArray]  -- "loop" scratch registers, evaluated once per step s in
//              [0,1] across `steps` subdivisions, per instance (C() macro).
//              Typically intermediate per-vertex math (radius*cos, etc.)
//              combining a[]/b[]/s/audio taps.
// x[MaxArray], y[MaxArray] -- final normalized device coordinates
//              (range roughly -1..1) written by X()/Y()/XY() macros, each
//              step; consumed by Draw() to emit a dot or polyline vertex.
// maxXY        -- highest index ever written to x[]/y[] (== xyiMax below);
//              Draw() renders vertices x[0..xyiMax], y[0..xyiMax].
//
// ---- runtime inputs available inside macro bodies (see CallTree.waves.md) ----
// t            current elapsed time in seconds (double; pixel/Waveshapes.cpp)
// s            step fraction 0..1 across the current shape's `steps`
// id, num      current instance index [0,num) and instance count
// ux,uy,ur,ua  user/UI control parameters (WaveShapes::userX/Y/R/A sliders)
// mag(s)       time-domain audio amplitude sampled at step position s
//              (WaveSky::mag -> waveFft.Tape[], i.e. oscilloscope trace)
// fft(s)       frequency-domain FFT bin intensity at position s
//              (WaveSky::fft -> waveFft.GetIntensity[])
// beat()       beat pulse accessor (WaveSky::beat(); stub returns 1 in the
//              current tree -- see CallTree.waves.md gap note)
// rnd(n)       uniform random in [0,n) (pixel/FieldFunc.cpp; seeded via
//              seed()/srand, consumed by many A()/B() setup terms)
// PI, sin/cos/pow/sqrt/... standard math; dabs/trnc/flor/wrap/clip/pos/sgn/
//              trwv/saw/sqwv/seed/sqr -- see pixel/FieldFunc.cpp
// timeStart()/timeEnd()/sampleSteps()/sampleSlots()/fftSlots()/fftSteps()
//              buffer/timing accessors (pixel/Waveshapes.cpp WaveShape class)
//
// DrawFn signature (represents WaveShape::draw(), pixel/Waveshapes.cpp:76):
//   connect==0 -> plot xyiMax+1 independent dots; connect==1 -> connect them
//   into a polyline (id used to keep each instance's poly indices distinct).
//   width<0 is clamped to 0.  If steps==1, dots are always used (connect
//   forced to 0) because there aren't enough points for a line.
// ============================================================================

